    "readmeSummary": "## Google Maps Scraper\n\nA scraper that extracts Google Maps business listings at scale by issuing the same data requests the Google Maps web client uses (no headless browser). It performs map-tile searches and deduplicates results across tiles and queries, optionally constraining searches to geographic boundaries from OpenStreetMap. For each found place it returns a single record containing business identity and categories, parsed address components, geographic coordinates and timezone, contact details (phone and website), reputation metrics (rating, review count, lead score, star-distribution), opening hours, structured \"About\" attributes (accessibility, payments, parking, service options), stable identifiers and map links, media references (main photo and photo counts, optional photo links), and optional full details including textual price ranges and up to eight reviews with author, rating, text and date. Additional optional processing reads a place’s website pages to extract emails, social profiles and detect contact forms. Designed for high-throughput searches (thousands of places per search) with per-place detailed fetches available on demand.\n\n## Use cases\n\n- Lead lists: compile lists of local businesses with phone numbers and websites, filterable by ratings or missing website.  \n- Market research: measure competitor counts, locations, ratings and price ranges across areas.  \n- Directory building: assemble names, structured addresses, hours, categories and stable place identifiers for directories.  \n- Monitoring: detect new businesses in an area or track rating and review-count changes over time.",
